setrow('AG','not_verified','Antigua requires permits and phytosanitary certificates for regulated plants, including some processed foods, in any quantity. Its published processing examples do not classify heat-processed retail Camellia tea.','All inbound consignments covered if regulated; no established small postal exemption.','Antigua and Barbuda Plant Protection Unit',['https://agriculture.gov.ag/index.php/plant-protection/','https://agriculture.gov.ag/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Import-Status-of-Plant-Commodities-and-Regulated-Items-PLANT-PROTECTION-ANTIGUA-AND-BARBUDA-ver.-27082020.pdf'],'Does the NPPO classify sealed steamed/dried sencha as regulated or sufficiently processed?')
setrow('KN','not_verified','Government guidance requires prior permits for unprocessed plant products and certificates/inspection for permitted small quantities. Its explicit dried-tea example is for exports, so it cannot establish an import requirement or exemption for sencha.','General public included, but postal finished-tea classification unresolved.','St Kitts and Nevis Department of Agriculture',['https://www.sknis.gov.kn/2020/06/26/plant-and-plant-product-import-requirements/'],'Confirm processed tea import category and any personal-post permit/certificate exemption.')
setrow('TT','not_verified','The ministry expressly applies plant permit and phytosanitary certificate controls to online and postal purchases. Regulations allow pest-safe preserved fruits/vegetables, but neither text resolves whether finished Camellia tea is outside regulated plant products.','Mail and courier explicitly covered for regulated products.','Trinidad and Tobago Plant Quarantine Service',['https://agriculture.gov.tt/media-releases/what-you-need-to-know-about-a-plant-import-permit/','https://www.ttbizlink.gov.tt/trade/tnt/cmn/pdf/Plant%20Protection%20Subsidiary%20Regulations-63.56.pdf'],'Obtain exact processed-tea classification; do not equate a raw-leaf permit rule with manufactured tea.')
setrow('BZ','permit_required','BAHA provides a processed-food import permit application explicitly covering personal consumption and mail/courier. Obtain BAHA clearance for the exact Japanese tea before shipment; additional plant certification depends on the issued conditions.','Personal consumption and Mail are express options on the 2025 form.','Belize Agricultural Health Authority',['https://baha.org.bz/food-safety/','https://baha.org.bz/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/FS-Permit.pdf'],'BAHA must specify any tea-specific plant certificate conditions; no automatic personal-use exemption located.')
setrow('AW','not_verified','Aruba food-import guidance lists tea for an economic import licence; this does not establish the agricultural treatment of small personal postal purchases.','Personal postal exemption and exact finished-tea agricultural classification not stated.','Aruba import requirements, reproduced by Germany JKI',['https://pflanzengesundheit.julius-kuehn.de/dokumente/upload/aw_2022_imp-req_en.pdf'],'Clarify personal postal tea licence scope and whether processed tea needs plant-health documentation.')
setrow('CW','not_verified','Curaçao customs requires permits for plants and flowers but does not classify manufactured dried tea. Personal goods customs clearance alone is insufficient agricultural evidence.','Traveler page and general import procedure reviewed; no tea-specific postal provision found.','Douane Curaçao',['https://douane.cw/particulier/reizigersbagage/verboden-in-en-uit-te-voeren/','https://douane.cw/zakelijk/inklaring-en-invoer/'],'Confirm agriculture exemption or requirements for commercially sealed Japanese tea sent by post.')
