setrow('KY','conditional','Department of Agriculture explicitly allows commercially packaged processed tea and coffee. Declare all food to Customs for agricultural inspection.','The commodity FAQ covers imports generally, rather than a baggage-only concession.','Cayman Islands Department of Agriculture',['https://doa.gov.ky/faqs/','https://doa.gov.ky/service/agricultural-health-inspection-services/'])
setrow('FK','conditional','Processed plant materials are permitted in sealed packaging identifying product, processing method, manufacturer and origin. Tea must be clean, manufactured and labelled; biosecurity can inspect.','General importer guidance applies to consignments. Passenger allowances are not used as parcel allowances.','Falkland Islands Department of Agriculture Biosecurity',['https://www.gov.fk/agriculture/wp-content/uploads/sites/28/2026/03/Importers-Guide-2020.pdf','https://www.gov.fk/agriculture/biosecurity/importing-exporting/'])
setrow('GU','not_verified','Guam regulation 10120 permits stored dried human foods subject to inspection and freedom from storage pests. Sections 10101 and 10103 separately require permits for regulated plant products; the text does not expressly say whether manufactured sencha needs that permit.','Territorial import rule covers shipments, not just passengers. Federal mainland tea rules cannot settle Guam permit interpretation.','Guam Department of Agriculture and Compiler of Laws',['https://www.guamcourts.org/compileroflaws/GAR/08GAR/08GAR002-10.pdf','https://doag.guam.gov/biosecurity-division/'],'Confirm whether sealed heat-processed dried tea under 10120 is non-regulated and permit-exempt.')
setrow('MP','not_verified','CNMI section 85-60.2-238 allows stored dried human food, subject to inspection and pest freedom. Sections 201/204 distinguish non-regulated goods from plant products needing permits; section 202 does not list dried foods for phytosanitary certificates.','CNMI Customs controls incoming US Postal Service goods; the dried-food entry rule is not baggage-only.','CNMI Law Revision Commission; Customs and Quarantine',['https://cnmilaw.gov/docs/admincode/T85/T85-60.2.pdf','https://www.finance.gov.mp/customs-quarantine.php'],'Confirm dried manufactured tea is a non-regulated food for permit purposes under sections 201/204/238.')
setrow('AS','permit_required','American Samoa plant quarantine rules require a prior permit for plant material, with origin certification and arrival inspection; definitions include plant products and no manufactured-tea exception was identified. Obtain the tea-specific permit before dispatch.','Import definition covers any person and shipment. No small personal postal waiver found.','American Samoa plant quarantine regulations, chapter 24.03',['https://faolex.fao.org/docs/pdf/ams68618.pdf','https://asbar.org/regulation/24-0328-permit-for-plant-material-importation/'],'Agriculture must confirm permit conditions and the required origin certificate for sealed Japanese sencha.')
setrow('NI','not_verified','NTON 11003, published January 2024, expressly covers all quantities, presentations, online purchases and postal consignments. Regulated consignments require importer registration, import permit and phytosanitary documentation. A finished-tea classification or processing exemption was not established.','Personal postal purchases expressly within the new standard; do not rely on the superseded 11005-08 rule.','Nicaragua IPSA',['https://www.ipsa.gob.ni/Portals/0/5%20Cuarentena%20Agropecuaria/Normas%20y%20procedimientos/Gaceta%2015.07.2024%20NTON%2011003.pdf'],'Does IPSA regard factory-steamed/dried Camellia tea as a regulated consignment requiring the NTON permit procedure?')
setrow('AR','not_verified','SENASA applies AFIDI plant requirements to regulated commercial and noncommercial consignments. Personal online food customs/ANMAT simplification does not determine whether this sencha is phytosanitary category 1 or 2.','Noncommercial consignments are expressly covered by SENASA; personal postal food rules must not be treated as plant-health clearance.','Argentina SENASA',['https://www.argentina.gob.ar/node/102592','https://www.argentina.gob.ar/normativa/nacional/resoluci%C3%B3n-12-2021-346384/actualizacion','https://www.argentina.gob.ar/node/455690'],'Confirm sencha processing category and whether a SENASA import request/AFIDI is required for a personal parcel.')
