setrow('PE','conditional','SENASA classifies loose green tea in retail packs of 3 kg or less (0902.10.00.00 P2) as phytosanitary risk category 2. Postal procedure 6.2.1 waives import permit and origin phytosanitary certificate, but requires inspection on arrival. A 100 g loose-leaf pouch is not the category-1 tea-filter/capsule exemption.','The official procedure is expressly for postal consignments. The 3 kg threshold describes immediate packaging for tariff classification, not a total personal allowance.','Peru SENASA',['https://www.senasa.gob.pe/senasa/descargasarchivos/2017/08/Listado-mercancias-agrarias-reguladas-09.12.2020.pdf','https://www.senasa.gob.pe/senasa/descargasarchivos/2014/11/49.pdf','https://www.senasa.gob.pe/senasa/descargasarchivos/2015/02/12.pdf'],'The July 2026 list landing page could not be retrieved; latest accessible detailed list and standing postal procedure agree on CRF2 treatment.')
setrow('UY','allowed','MGAP public database lists PRODUCTOS VEGETALES ACONDICIONADOS AL DETALLE, explicitly including tea, among products without entry controls. Sealed 100 g retail sencha matches that commodity; do not extend this conclusion to bulk raw leaves.','The entry-control exemption is a general commodity classification, not a traveler allowance.','Uruguay MGAP DGSA',['https://www.mgap.gub.uy/consultaRequisitos/requisitosincontrol.aspx','https://www.gub.uy/ministerio-ganaderia-agricultura-pesca/tramites-y-servicios/servicios/consulta-requisitos-para-ingreso-productos-vegetales'],attempts=['Opened MGAP public no-control database; extracted current embedded result row 4047 / PVDET19999100 expressly listing retail tea.'])
setrow('BS','not_verified','BAHFSA explicitly lists tea for agricultural declaration/inspection. Its general plant rules require permit and phytosanitary certificate, including mail/courier. Guidance does not resolve whether sealed industrially processed tea is exempt from the raw/minimally processed category.','Mail, couriers and freight forwarders expressly covered by plant rules; traveler tea declaration is not proof of a postal permit waiver.','Bahamas Agricultural Health and Food Safety Authority',['https://bahfsabahamas.com/sectors/plants/faqs','https://bahfsabahamas.com/sectors/international/guidelines-for-the-importation-of-plants-and-plant-products','https://bahfsabahamas.com/downloads/documents/legislation/Food-Import-Conditions-Appendix.pdf'],'Ask BAHFSA whether manufactured tea requires the individual permit and phytosanitary certificate; do not ship under a presumed small-quantity exemption.')
setrow('BB','not_verified','Barbados provides a plant import-permit procedure, including personal consumption and mail selections. Plant regulation applicability to sufficiently processed manufactured tea was not determined; a draft replacement Act is not treated as enacted law.','Personal/mail options establish that individual parcels can be regulated; they do not prove that sencha is regulated or exempt.','Barbados Ministry of Agriculture Plant Quarantine',['https://agriculture.gov.bb/Apply/ImportationOfPlants'],'Confirm finished Camellia tea classification under the operative Plant Protection Act and any permit/certificate exemption.')
setrow('JM','not_verified','Jamaica plant quarantine guidance provides permits, original phytosanitary documentation and inspection for regulated plant products, with a personal JSWIFT application route. No tea-specific processed-product exemption was verified.','Personal import route identified; no evidence that a baggage concession exempts commercial mail purchases.','Jamaica Ministry of Agriculture Plant Quarantine',['https://www.moa.gov.jm/sites/default/files/Import-Requirement-and-Permit-Application-Process.pdf','https://www.moa.gov.jm/sites/default/files/Import%20Process%20BROCHURE.pdf'],'Obtain PQPI classification and any Japanese sencha permit requirements; website commodity table could not be retrieved.')
setrow('LC','not_verified','Saint Lucia regulates processed or unprocessed vegetable-origin articles capable of carrying pests. Regulation 16 requires permits and regulation 12 expressly covers mail. Sealed heat-processed tea is not specifically classified in published guidance.','Mail is expressly subject to the plant regulations; no personal parcel exemption established.','Saint Lucia Attorney General and Plant Quarantine',['https://attorneygeneralchambers.com/laws-of-saint-lucia/plant-protection-act/section-2-02','https://attorneygeneralchambers.com/laws-of-saint-lucia/plant-protection-act/section-16-01','https://attorneygeneralchambers.com/laws-of-saint-lucia/plant-protection-act/section-12'],'Does the authority consider manufactured dried sencha capable of carrying pests, and thus a regulated plant product?')
