setrow('EC','conditional','Andean Resolution 1475 lists retail green tea as risk category 2; the default is no import permit or phytosanitary export certificate, with arrival inspection. National product-specific exceptions can override this general rule. Declare manufactured tea accurately and retain processing/origin details.','Resolution expressly covers trade with third countries, not only Andean trade or passenger baggage; therefore relevant to Japanese postal parcels.','Ecuador Agrocalidad / Andean Community',['https://www.agrocalidad.gob.ec/wp-content/uploads/2020/05/fito30.pdf','https://www.agrocalidad.gob.ec/direccion-de-control-fitosanitario/'],'No Japan-sencha-specific national exception was located; confirm the commodity entry with Agrocalidad before operational rollout.')
setrow('CR','not_verified','Costa Rica requires plant-health clearance for regulated NT35 goods. The public requirement database distinguishes processed leaves, dried leaves and tea infusions, but Japan queries failed and did not establish which requirements apply to this retail product.','No personal-post exemption established; commodity classification must precede any permit requirement.','Costa Rica Servicio Fitosanitario del Estado',['https://www.sfe.go.cr/SitePages/Tramites/tramites_importacion_vegetales.aspx','https://app.sfe.go.cr/SFECuarentena/aspx/RequisitosImportacion/ConsultarRequisitosImportacion.aspx'],'Obtain the Japan/Camellia sinensis/processed-leaf commodity result and clarify NT35 scope.',attempts=['Read import guidance and current public query form. Attempted Japan processed-leaf and dry-leaf searches; server returned unspecified system errors.'])
setrow('DM','not_verified','Dominica plant import guidance requires prior permission, export phytosanitary certification and inspection for regulated plant material. The Act exempts certain preserved fruits/vegetables but does not specifically classify manufactured Camellia tea.','Individual import procedure exists; no personal postal tea exemption established.','Dominica Ministry of Agriculture',['https://establishment.gov.dm/services/application-import-permit','https://divisionofagriculture.gov.dm/images/documents/forms/sample_import_permit_and_submission_form.pdf','https://faolex.fao.org/docs/pdf/dmi4119.pdf'],'Confirm whether heat-processed retail sencha is regulated and requires permit/phyto for postal entry.')
setrow('GD','not_verified','Grenada plant controls require permits and plant-health certification for regulated plant products. Published import summaries did not establish that fully manufactured sencha falls within that category or has a personal-mail exemption.','No affirmative postal tea allowance verified; tariff availability does not establish plant-health clearance.','Grenada Ministry of Agriculture; government-notified WTO trade policy review',['https://www.wto.org/english/tratop_e/tpr_e/s299-02_e.pdf','https://www.ippc.int/en/countries/grenada/'],'Obtain NPPO ruling on manufactured Japanese tea and personal postal permit/certificate requirements.')
setrow('VC','not_verified','The 2015 Plant Protection Act provides for interception of plant consignments by the postal corporation and private postal providers. Import licensing applies to regulated plant products; no tea-specific manufacturing exemption was verified.','Postal channels expressly covered by section 15; no personal quantity exception established for this tea.','St Vincent and the Grenadines Plant Protection and Quarantine',['https://faolex.fao.org/docs/pdf/stv160536.pdf','https://importlicensing.wto.org/content/plant-and-plant-products-2'],'Confirm whether factory-steamed/dried tea is regulated and the exact personal postal permit/certificate conditions.')
setrow('MS','not_verified','Montserrat Plant Protection Act controls regulated plants and products; its preserved-fruit exceptions do not expressly settle processed tea. The government confirms current agricultural permit administration following 2025 amendments, which concern citrus rather than tea.','No manufactured-tea exemption for individual post found in law or current guidance.','Montserrat Department of Agriculture',['https://faolex.fao.org/docs/pdf/msr98141.pdf','https://www.gov.ms/2025/03/07/citrus-fruits-now-allowed-for-importation-to-montserrat/'],'Confirm finished tea classification, permit/certificate requirements and any personal-post exemption.')
setrow('TC','not_verified','Turks and Caicos requires permits for regulated plant articles; only fruits/vegetables have the published 25 lb threshold. Manufactured tea is not classified in that guidance, so neither blanket permit necessity nor exemption is proven.','General individual/company imports covered; do not apply the 25 lb produce threshold to tea or invent a postal exemption.','Turks and Caicos Department of Agriculture',['https://gov.tc/trade/portal/imports','https://www.agriculture.gov.tc/residents'],'Does commercially sealed heat-processed sencha fall outside regulated articles; if not, which permit/certificate conditions apply?')
