setrow('GT','not_verified','MAGA administers plant import permits under its plant-health law and import procedures, but the public product lookup did not establish the Japanese manufactured-tea classification. Regional Central American exemptions cannot be assumed to cover Japan.','No personal postal tea exemption verified in the published permit procedure or SEPA manual.','Guatemala MAGA VISAR',['https://www.tramites.gob.gt/servicio/2824/','https://www.maga.gob.gt/sitios/visar/facilitacion-de-comercio/','https://www.maga.gob.gt/sitios/visar/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Manual-SEPA.pdf','https://sigie.maga.gob.gt/ConsultaProducto?tipo=2'],'Confirm processed Camellia tea from Japan and its personal-post permit/certificate requirements.',attempts=['Reviewed the official permit service, VISAR trade facilitation guidance, 2025 SEPA manual and SIGIE product lookup. No product-and-origin result confirming finished sencha was available.'])
setrow('HN','not_verified','Enacted SENASA quarantine regulation 001-2023 articles 5–12 applies permits and specified certification to regulated imports for commercial or other purposes, including consumption. Article 11 provides exempt-product lists; a matching finished-tea exemption or Japan commodity entry was not located.','Individual consumption is expressly included in permit applications; no postal small-quantity waiver established.','Honduras SENASA; Tribunal Superior de Cuentas official gazette',['https://www.tsc.gob.hn/web/leyes/Acuerdo-CD-SENASA-001-2023.pdf','https://sistemas.senasa.gob.hn/senasa/index.php/sub-direcciones/sub-direccion-tecnica-de-sanidad-vegetal/requisitos-fitosanitarios-para-la-importacion-de-vegetales'],'Does manufactured Japanese sencha appear on an article 11 exemption list, and otherwise which permit/phyto conditions apply?',attempts=['Read enacted 2023 regulation, specifically articles 7 and 11, and country commodity requirement tables; rejected the earlier 2022 draft as legal authority. No Japan/tea entry established.'])
setrow('SV','not_verified','MAG import authorization applies to regulated plant products. The March 2025 customs/MAG update still requires phytosanitary certificates for items labelled tea extract and powdered tea, but neither is the 090210 loose sencha product. A general processed-food exemption is therefore unsafe.','No confirmed personal postal exemption. The 2025 list covers small samples as well as other goods; small quantity alone is not clearance.','El Salvador MAG; Dirección General de Aduanas',['https://www.mag.gob.sv/guia-para-autorizaciones-de-importacion-de-productos-y-subproductos-de-origen-vegetal-en-el-centro-de-importaciones-y-exportaciones-de-el-salvador-ciex-el-salvador/','https://sitio.aduana.gob.sv/download/anexo-1-del-boletin-informativo-no-dga-003-2025/','https://sitio.aduana.gob.sv/wp-content/uploads/download-manager-files/ANEXO-1-BOLETIN-INF-No.-DGA-003-2025.pdf'],'Obtain MAG classification for HS 090210 loose manufactured tea, rather than extending the extract/powder entries.',attempts=['Reviewed MAG authorization procedure and current customs March 2025 MAG update (landing page updated April 2026). Distinguished tea entries under 2101/2103 from the product under 090210.'])
setrow('SR','not_verified','Suriname renewed its requirement for prior plant import permits, original phytosanitary certification and inspection in August 2026. Its guidance defines plant products in terms of unprocessed pest-bearing material; manufactured sencha is not explicitly classified.','General import notice contains no personal-post exemption; noncommercial plant imports are covered if regulated.','Suriname Ministry of Agriculture, Livestock and Fisheries NPPO',['https://gov.sr/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Procedure-voor-de-invoer-van-planten-en-plantaardige-producten.jpg','https://gov.sr/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/LVV-IDB-Nieuwsbrief-uitgave-02.pdf'],'Does the NPPO classify steamed/dried retail tea as a regulated plant product under the 2020 Act?',attempts=['Read and OCRed the 14 August 2026 official import procedure notice, then compared the 2023 government explanation of plant-product scope. The finished-tea classification remains unresolved.'])
setrow('VG','not_verified','British Virgin Islands plant import conditions require a prior permit and phytosanitary certificate, but the published detailed conditions concern nursery plants, roots and growing material. That is not sufficient to classify manufactured dried tea as permit-controlled.','No personal postal processed-tea exception or explicit classification found.','British Virgin Islands Department of Agriculture',['https://bvi.gov.vg/sites/default/files/CONDITIONS%20FOR%20PLANT%20IMPORTATION.pdf','https://www.bvi.gov.vg/tags/agriculture?page=17'],'Confirm whether heat-processed retail tea is outside plant import controls or needs a permit and certificate.',attempts=['Read official plant-import conditions and agriculture notices; searched for tea/personal-mail scope. Excluded the draft Food Security and Sustainability Act from operative-law evidence.'])
setrow('GL','not_verified','Greenland has separate import arrangements; Danish or EU mainland plant-health exemptions cannot establish Greenland postal tea admissibility. Official Greenland food-import guidance did not settle the agricultural status of manufactured Camellia tea.','The available personal-food page is traveler-focused and is not extended to a Japanese online parcel.','Greenland food-import guidance from Danish Veterinary and Food Administration',['https://foedevarestyrelsen.dk/indgange/groenland/groenlandske-foedevarer/mad-med-paa-rejsen','https://foedevarestyrelsen.dk/indgange/groenland/groenlandske-foedevarer/indfoersel-samhandel-og-eksport/indfoersel-fra-tredjelande-og-graensekontrol'],'Identify the applicable Greenland plant-health rule and confirm sealed tea by post from Japan.',attempts=['Searched Naalakkersuisut and Greenland-specific Danish authority guidance for plant-health, tea and postal food imports; available travel and food-control material did not establish this plant-health route.'])
setrow('BL','not_verified','Saint Barthélemy operates territorial plant-import controls and invasive-species restrictions. The authority forms and plant allowlists concern flora and do not establish the treatment of manufactured tea; metropolitan EU tea rules are not substituted.','No verified personal-post rule for heat-processed Camellia tea.','Saint Barthélemy Agence Territoriale de l’Environnement',['https://www.agencedelenvironnement.fr/en/page/Identify-invasive-exotic-species','https://www.agencedelenvironnement.fr/en/page/promoting-native-flora','https://www.agencedelenvironnement.fr/en/formulaire/2'],'Does sealed manufactured tea fall outside the territorial plant permit system, and are any certificates needed?',attempts=['Reviewed ATE territorial invasive-plant rules, native-flora guidance and plant authorization forms; no processed-tea or personal-post provision found.'])
setrow('MF','not_verified','Saint Martin is outside the EU plant-health territory. A Dutch NPPO country sheet lists specific dried plant goods needing certification, but does not list tea and dates its substantive rules to 2012; that cannot verify the present Japanese postal route.','No current local manufactured-tea/personal-post confirmation; do not use mainland French rules automatically.','Netherlands NVWA country requirements for Saint Martin; French plant-health law',['https://www.nvwa.nl/site/binaries/site-content/collections/documents/fytosanitair/landeneisen/diverse-producten/saint-martin-diverse-producten-exporteisen/Saint-Martin_Diverse_producten_exporteisen_1.0.pdf','https://www.legifrance.gouv.fr/loda/id/JORFTEXT000000343648/'],'Confirm current Saint Martin applicability and finished-tea treatment for direct Japanese personal mail.',attempts=['Reviewed the full NVWA Saint Martin country sheet, including its 2012/2013 revision history and third-country plant-product list; searched French local import guidance. Current tea-specific scope remains unverified.'])
for code,local in [('GF','https://daaf.guyane.agriculture.gouv.fr/IMG/pdf/900903_controle_vgtx_cle026c57.pdf'),('GP','https://daaf.guadeloupe.agriculture.gouv.fr/l-envoi-de-vegetaux-de-la-guadeloupe-vers-la-france-et-les-autres-pays-de-l-a1199.html'),('MQ','https://daaf.martinique.agriculture.gouv.fr/importation-des-vegetaux-et-produits-vegetaux-a362.html')]:
 setrow(code,'not_verified','The French overseas 3 September 1990 plant-health order defines controlled plant products by processing and listed commodity. Its special dried-tea entry is restricted to Réunion; that condition must not be imposed here. Current local classification of manufactured Japanese sencha has not been established.','These destinations are separate from the EU plant-health territory. Neither metropolitan EU clearance nor a passenger allowance proves this personal postal route.','French Ministry of Agriculture; local DAAF',['https://www.legifrance.gouv.fr/loda/id/JORFTEXT000000343648/',local],'Confirm that heat-processed retail sencha is outside the locally controlled commodity list and whether any personal-post documentation applies.',attempts=['Read the 1990 overseas plant-health order and its territory-specific dried-tea entry; reviewed local DAAF guidance. The Réunion-only condition does not settle this territory’s current manufactured-tea scope.'])
setrow('PM','not_verified','Saint Pierre and Miquelon has its own Code rural plant-import authorization and certification framework, with plant products defined by limited processing. The local Newfoundland exception does not cover direct Japanese parcels. No manufactured-sencha classification was established.','Rules are territory-specific; professional registration requirements alone do not resolve individual mail permits.','French Code rural, Saint Pierre and Miquelon provisions; prefecture',['https://www.legifrance.gouv.fr/codes/section_lc/LEGITEXT000006071367/LEGISCTA000032693959/','https://www.legifrance.gouv.fr/codes/article_lc/LEGIARTI000035419827','https://www.saint-pierre-et-miquelon.gouv.fr/contenu/telechargement/812/4383/file/Recueil%20administratif%20%20-%20Septembre%202009.pdf'],'Does steamed/dried retail sencha fall outside regulated unprocessed/simply prepared plant products; if not, which personal-post authorizations apply?',attempts=['Reviewed current territory-specific Code rural provisions D274-26 onwards and the prefectural import order; distinguished professional registration and Newfoundland concessions from the Japanese personal postal case.'])
setrow('EC','permit_required','Ecuador’s national COMEX 009-2022 row 616 explicitly requires an Agrocalidad import permit and DDA for retail green tea (090210). The quarantine manual requires operator registration, prior permit, origin certification and arrival inspection for regulated postal consignments. A processed-product exemption requires an Agrocalidad categorization decision; it cannot be assumed from the general Andean category alone.','Quarantine manual section 9 expressly covers natural persons using postal/courier services. The separate 1 kg traveler allowance is not applied to mail.','Ecuador Agrocalidad; COMEX',['https://www.agrocalidad.gob.ec/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/2RESOL1.pdf','https://www.agrocalidad.gob.ec/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/Resol_133_Manual-general-de-cuarentena-vegetal.pdf','https://www.agrocalidad.gob.ec/direccion-de-control-fitosanitario/'],'Request Agrocalidad categorization for this manufactured sencha if seeking exemption; absent that decision follow the retail-green-tea permit entry.',attempts=['Cross-checked Andean Resolution 1475 against the national COMEX tariff list: row 616 expressly controls 090210. Read quarantine manual section 9 on postal consignments and its processed-product categorization note, and rejected the baggage-only 1 kg allowance.'])
save()
