setrow('CL','conditional','Japan’s current NPPO postal table explicitly marks manufactured green tea to Chile ◎: no Japanese phytosanitary export certificate required. SAG category-1 guidance supports entry of sufficiently processed plant foods; retain the sealed finished-tea packaging and manufacturing description for any inspection. This conclusion is for manufactured sencha, not raw merely dried leaf material.','The 21 April 2026 MAFF table expressly covers postal shipments. No agricultural personal tea weight cap was identified.','Japan MAFF Plant Protection Station, reporting Chilean requirements; Chile SAG',['https://www.maff.go.jp/pps/j/search/e_hayami_yubin.pdf','https://www.maff.go.jp/pps/j/search/ekuni/sa/chile/index.html','https://www.sag.gob.cl/sites/default/files/res._1.284_de_2021_con_anexo.pdf'],'SAG’s table separately names dried-and-crushed tea; the exact Japanese manufactured-green-tea postal guidance supplies the product-specific clearance. Preserve steaming/finished-product evidence if SAG requests classification.',attempts=['Read SAG processing categories and the current Japanese NPPO postal matrix. Reconciled the dried-and-crushed example with the explicit manufactured-green-tea ◎ entry on the first page (Chile is printed as spaced チ リ).'])
setrow('GF','not_verified','Guyane order R03-2021-04-26-00003 bans personal imports of regulated plants/plant products in any quantity from all origins, subject to an approved derogation. Its scope uses the 1990 definition of unprocessed or simply prepared plant products. Whether steaming/manufacturing removes this retail sencha from that definition remains unresolved.','The order covers personal introduction/importation broadly, not merely a passenger allowance; no postal exemption established.','Guyane prefecture/DGTM; French Ministry of Agriculture',['https://www.guyane.gouv.fr/content/download/18708/131303/file/recueil-r03-2021-109-recueil-des-actes-administratifs.pdf','https://www.legifrance.gouv.fr/loda/id/JORFTEXT000000343648/','https://info.agriculture.gouv.fr/boagri/instruction-2025-102/telechargement'],'Confirm finished heat-processed sencha is outside the 1990 plant-product definition; otherwise obtain the local prior derogation before any personal parcel.',attempts=['Read the 1990 overseas rule and 2025 ministry instruction retaining pre-2019 law pending an overseas decree. Located the official 2021 personal-import order; the official PDF was inaccessible, so checked its reproduced legal text (articles 1–2) against the official indexed title and number. No 2025/2026 processed-tea exemption found.'])
setrow('MQ','not_verified','Martinique DAAF expressly cites the 22 November 2004 order prohibiting personal plant-product imports from all origins, using the 1990 definition of unprocessed or simply prepared material. The effect on factory-steamed/dried sencha is not explicitly resolved; the Réunion-specific dried-tea rule is not applied here.','The local rule concerns personal introductions/imports generally; no manufactured-tea postal exception established.','Martinique DAAF; French Ministry of Agriculture',['https://daaf.martinique.agriculture.gouv.fr/quels-sont-les-vegetaux-soumis-a-un-contole-au-pec-lors-de-leur-introduction-a373.html','https://daaf.martinique.agriculture.gouv.fr/importation-des-vegetaux-et-produits-vegetaux-a362.html','https://www.legifrance.gouv.fr/loda/id/JORFTEXT000000343648/','https://info.agriculture.gouv.fr/boagri/instruction-2025-102/telechargement'],'Obtain DAAF confirmation that finished manufactured sencha is outside the regulated plant-product definition and personal-import restriction.',attempts=['Reviewed the DAAF controlled-goods FAQ expressly citing the 2004 personal-import ban, the 1990 product definition and the ministry’s 2025 transitional-law instruction. Searched current local processing exclusions without finding a finished-tea ruling.'])
